From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:48:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] MiniMax-M3.1-Flash: fix the rows contract test's decode
 aliasing, simulate the norm's sums, add mm3-contract (T8d)

The spark2 failure "v was not stored as it came" at 8x32x1 was a test bug: the decode
window put every row at position 0 (k 1) behind one shared table, so 8 CTAs wrote one
(page, slot) and one survived. Each decode row now owns its table (row_tab) and page.
The twin gains a test that flags the planted alias. The rows kernel does have fp32 sums
(the norm's sum of squares), so the spec keeps accum f32 and the writer now simulates
them for gate 4. tf-cuda-test mm3-contract runs every MiniMax kernel through gates 1-4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QguKy82jHfqdgzDsrrC5xs
